  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection in Practice (PiP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To act in accordance with PoC policy and mitigate civilian harm, military personnel need to be adequately trained and equipped, and possess knowledge of both their responsibilities and the operating context. The PiP project seeks to meet the diverse information needs of military actors and institutions. PAX contributes to PoC-focused trainings and exercises grounded in field realities. We also advise missions and disseminate best practices regarding data-driven decision making and evaluating the effectiveness of military interventions. Finally, we facilitate transparency and accountability of military missions by promoting clear guidelines and methods for tracking, reporting and responding to civilian harm incidents.</narrative>
  </description>
